alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn main(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "firn, a server of Redis's protocol for the commands firn/README.md lists, over TCP in RESP2 or RESP3 or as inline commands, with pipelining. It serves each accepted client in a context of its own over one keyspace, a shared state every client reaches through atomic statements that hold the entries of the keys a command names, or the keyspace's map whole for DBSIZE. Its invocation reads an optional Redis configuration file or stdin -, followed by --directive values. Later directives override the file, maxclients defaults to 10000 and refuses excess connected clients with Redis's error; --firn-clients is a test-only served-client limit, and invalid configuration prints its reason and exits 1. Include and directory changes beyond dir . or ./ are refused explicitly pending firn-req-host-paths. firn listens on the address --bind names, the loopback address by default. An append-only file is replayed before firn listens and every change is appended to it, the file synced once a second. A client without active subscriptions silent for the idle limit, when it is not zero, is closed, and while a password is required a client must give it before other commands. Expired keys are removed when a command finds them and by a context that wakes ten times a second. SIGTERM and SIGINT, heard from before the append-only file's replay, request the orderly stop SHUTDOWN requests, after which a further signal ends firn at once; a request the replay sees, at most 1024 commands after it is made, ends firn with status 0, leaving appendonlydir as the replay found it, as Redis 7.2.16 exits while it loads. firn stops with status 3 when the host refuses it those signals, before it replays anything, or when it cannot listen on its address.";
